\description{
Density & Distribution Function variable-knot Spline (DDFS) estimation is a
non-parametric method for estimating the pdf and the cdf of an unknown univariate
or multivariate distribution based on a given data sample. Fits with two or more
dimensions require a multidimensional build of GeDS. Above two dimensions,
missing tuning parameters use provisional fixed defaults; see
\code{\link{ddfs}} for their values and the current limitations.
